=== WITNESS CORRECTION (docs-gate-engineer, verified by me) ===
The lesson I passed to docs-gate-engineer cited `evidence/pack-closure/verify/20260917T024741Z/raw/pass2.stdout.log` as the 0-byte failure snapshot of the mpd-bg launch shape. That path now holds the SUCCESSFUL pass-2 output (2,435 B, mtime 10:57:02 local) because MY OWN successful re-run redirected the driver's stdout onto the same path — so the failure witness was destroyed by the fix it justified. Verified here.
CAUSE, owned: the failing launch wrote `pass2.stdout.log` via mpd-bg (0 B) and the next call re-ran the same driver with `> $D/raw/pass2.stdout.log`, overwriting it.
SURVIVING WITNESSES for the launch bound: (1) `scripts/mpd-bg.mjs:89` — the helper's own note ("start this INSIDE a managed background job — a detached child dies with its bwrap sandbox otherwise (T-23)"); (2) the session's job output for the failed attempt (0-byte log + a pidfile probing RUNNING while `ps` showed nothing = a reaped child); (3) the REPRODUCIBLE probe re-run under `launch-probe/` in this board directory (added after run 1), which preserves its own 0-byte log, its absent marker and its DEAD probe reading with a hash-qualified citation.
RULE going forward: a witness that a later run can overwrite must be copied or hash-quoted at the moment it is read; prose is not a witness.

